+# Portfolio recovery + release runbook
+
+## What happened with the missing pages
+A few content pages and project entries disappeared during portfolio edits/recovery work. Based on the repo history and notes from 2026-03-18, the main failure mode was not "GitHub lost files" — it was us shipping page/content changes without enough safety rails.
+
+Recovered work that had to be restored:
+- services catalog + workspace/domain setup page
+- services navigation
+- support + managed hosting service detail pages
+- missing project entries (`Custom AI Agent Setup`, `AI Agent Orchestrator`)
+- contact-form success handling fix
+- removal of the broken embedded Google Calendar booking iframe
+
+## Why this can happen again if we stay sloppy
+1. Content lives in multiple places (`pages/`, `data/projectsData.ts`, nav links, static assets).
+2. A route can still compile while the linked content silently disappears.
+3. GitHub Pages will happily publish a broken-but-building site.
+4. Direct-to-main pushes remove the review checkpoint.
+
+## New rules
+1. **No direct feature work on `main`.**
+   - `main` = production
+   - `develop` = always-on preview / review branch
+   - feature branches branch off `develop`
+2. **Every change comes through a PR.**
+3. **Eddie reviews on the dev site before merge to `main`.**
+4. **CI must pass before merge.**
+5. **Any route/data/content change must include test coverage or a smoke test update.**
+
+## Branch flow
+- Create feature branch from `develop`
+- Open PR into `develop`
+- CI runs tests + build
+- GitHub Action publishes `develop` preview to:
+  - `https://eddiemoger.com/dev/`
+- Eddie reviews preview
+- Merge to `develop`
+- When approved for production, open PR from `develop` -> `main`
+- After merge to `main`, deploy production
+
+## Minimum checks for route/content changes
+- `npm test -- --watchAll=false`
+- `npm run build`
+- Visit changed page(s)
+- Verify no project/service entries disappeared
+- Verify any new links/routes are reachable
+
+## Testing added specifically to prevent silent breakage
+- route smoke tests for major pages
+- data integrity tests for unique project ids/slugs and required content fields
+
+## Important deployment note
+Production is still GitHub Pages for `eddiemoger.com`.
+The preview workflow publishes a review build into `/dev/` on the `gh-pages` branch so preview work stays visible without replacing production root content.
+
+## Recommended repo settings (manual admin step)
+These require repo admin access in GitHub settings:
+- protect `main`
+- require pull request before merge
+- require at least 1 approval
+- require status checks: `CI / test-and-build`
+- optionally restrict who can push directly to `main`
+- optionally enable auto-delete head branches after merge
+
+## AI review tools
+Good options:
+- **CodeRabbit** for PR summaries/review suggestions
+- **GitHub Copilot code review** if enabled on the repo/account
+
+These require installing/configuring a GitHub App in repo settings, so they were not fully auto-enabled from this workspace session.
